/-!
# The Lazard ring, its universal formal group law and its grading

A one-dimensional formal group law `F(X, Y)` over a commutative ring `R` satisfies `F(X, 0) = X`
and `F(0, Y) = Y`, so it has the shape

  `F(X, Y) = X + Y + ∑_{i, j ≥ 1} aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ`

and is determined by its coefficients `aᵢⱼ ∈ R`. Conversely, for a family `a` of coefficients the
power series `TauCeti.lazardSeries a = X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` is a commutative formal group law
exactly when the coefficients of `G(G(X, Y), Z) - G(X, G(Y, Z))` and of `G(X, Y) - G(Y, X)` vanish.
These coefficients are integral polynomials in the `aᵢⱼ`, so commutative formal group laws over
`R` are the ring homomorphisms to `R` from the **Lazard ring**

  `L = ℤ[aᵢⱼ | i, j ≥ 1] ⧸ (the coefficients of associativity and commutativity)`.

The images of the variables `aᵢⱼ` in `L` form the coefficients of a commutative formal group law
over `L`, the **universal formal group law**, and every commutative formal group law over `R` is
its base change along exactly one ring homomorphism `L →+* R`.

Give `aᵢⱼ` the homological degree `2 (i + j - 1)`: this is the degree of the corresponding
coefficient of the formal group law of a complex oriented cohomology theory, whose orientation has
cohomological degree `2`. The coefficients of associativity and commutativity are homogeneous for
this weighting, so `L` is graded, `L = ⨁ₙ Lₙ`. Homogeneity is proved with the rescaling
`F^s(X, Y) = s⁻¹ F(s X, s Y)` (`FormalGroup.rescale`): rescaling the universal formal group law by
`T²` over `L[T]` is classified by a ring homomorphism `L → L[T]` sending the class of `aᵢⱼ` to
`T ^ (2 (i + j - 1)) aᵢⱼ`, and the coefficient of `Tⁿ` in its value on the class of a polynomial is
the class of the homogeneous component of degree `n` of that polynomial. The universal property
then has a graded form: for a commutative ring `A` graded by `𝒜`, the homomorphism `L →+* A`
classifying a commutative formal group law over `A` is graded exactly when the coefficient of
`Xⁱ Yʲ` lies in `𝒜 (2 (i + j - 1))` for all `i, j`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.lazardSeries a`: the power series `X + Y + ∑_{i, j ≥ 1} aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.relations`: the ideal of `ℤ[aᵢⱼ]` generated by the coefficients of
  associativity and commutativity of the generic series `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing`: the Lazard ring, the quotient of `ℤ[aᵢⱼ]` by these relations, with
  quotient map `TauCeti.LazardRing.mk`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.formalGroup`: the universal commutative formal group law over the Lazard
  ring.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.lift`: the bijection between commutative formal group laws over `R` and ring
  homomorphisms `LazardRing →+* R`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.degree`: the homological degree `2 (i + j - 1)` of `aᵢⱼ`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.grading`: the grading of the Lazard ring by homological degree, with its
  `GradedAlgebra` instance.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.gradedLift`: the bijection between commutative formal group laws over a graded
  ring whose coefficients are homogeneous of the matching degrees and graded ring homomorphisms out
  of the Lazard ring.

## Main results

* `FormalGroup.coeff_single_zero`, `FormalGroup.coeff_single_one`: the coefficients of `Xⁿ` and
  `Yⁿ` in a formal group law are `1` for `n = 1` and `0` otherwise.
* `TauCeti.coeff_lazardSeries_eq`: the coefficient of an arbitrary monomial in
  `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ`.
* `TauCeti.lazardSeries_coeff_toPowerSeries`: every formal group law is the series
  `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` of its coefficients.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.coeff_formalGroup`: the coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in the universal formal
  group law is the class of `aᵢⱼ`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.map_lift`: the universal formal group law base-changes along `lift F` to `F`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.hom_ext`: a ring homomorphism out of the Lazard ring is determined by the
  base change of the universal formal group law along it.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.lift_map`: the bijection is natural in the coefficient ring.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.isHomogeneous_relations`: the ideal of Lazard relations is homogeneous.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.coeff_formalGroup_mem_grading`: the coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in the universal
  formal group law has degree `2 (i + j - 1)`.
* `TauCeti.LazardRing.lift_mem_iff`: the homomorphism classifying `F` is graded exactly when the
  coefficients of `F` are homogeneous of the matching degrees, for a target graded over any
  commutative monoid receiving the degrees of `L`, such as `ℤ`.

## References

* M. Lazard, *Sur les groupes de Lie formels à un paramètre*, Bull. Soc. Math. France 83 (1955).
* D. C. Ravenel, *Complex Cobordism and Stable Homotopy Groups of Spheres*, Appendix A2.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open MvPowerSeries Finsupp

namespace FormalGroup

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (F : FormalGroup R)

/-- The coefficient of `Xⁿ` in a formal group law `F(X, Y)`: since `F(X, 0) = X`, it is `1` for
`n = 1` and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem coeff_single_zero (n : ℕ) :
    coeff (single 0 n) F.toPowerSeries = if n = 1 then 1 else 0 := by
  rw [← coeff_subst_X_zero, ← Xzero, Xzero_eq_X, PowerSeries.coeff_X]

/-- The coefficient of `Yⁿ` in a formal group law `F(X, Y)`: since `F(0, Y) = Y`, it is `1` for
`n = 1` and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem coeff_single_one (n : ℕ) :
    coeff (single 1 n) F.toPowerSeries = if n = 1 then 1 else 0 := by
  rw [← coeff_subst_zero_X, ← zeroX, zeroX_eq_X, PowerSeries.coeff_X]

end FormalGroup

namespace TauCeti

section Semiring

variable {A B : Type*} [Semiring A] [Semiring B]

/-- The power series `X + Y + ∑_{i, j ≥ 1} aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` in two variables, for a family `a` of
coefficients indexed by pairs of positive integers. -/
def lazardSeries (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) A := fun d ↦
  if d 0 ≠ 0 ∧ d 1 ≠ 0 then a ((d 0).toPNat', (d 1).toPNat')
  else if d 0 + d 1 = 1 then 1 else 0

/-- The coefficient of an arbitrary monomial `X^(d 0) Y^(d 1)` in `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ`: it is
`aᵢⱼ` when both exponents are positive, `1` for the monomials `X` and `Y`, and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem coeff_lazardSeries_eq (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) (d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ) :
    coeff d (lazardSeries a) =
      if d 0 ≠ 0 ∧ d 1 ≠ 0 then a ((d 0).toPNat', (d 1).toPNat')
      else if d 0 + d 1 = 1 then 1 else 0 :=
  coeff_apply _ _

/-- The coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` is `aᵢⱼ` for `i, j ≥ 1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_lazardSeries (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) (i j : ℕ+) :
    coeff (single 0 (i : ℕ) + single 1 (j : ℕ)) (lazardSeries a) = a (i, j) := by
  simp [coeff_lazardSeries_eq]

/-- The coefficient of `Xⁿ` in `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` is `1` for `n = 1` and `0` otherwise. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_single_zero_lazardSeries (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) (n : ℕ) :
    coeff (single 0 n) (lazardSeries a) = if n = 1 then 1 else 0 := by
  simp [coeff_lazardSeries_eq]

/-- The coefficient of `Yⁿ` in `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` is `1` for `n = 1` and `0` otherwise. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_single_one_lazardSeries (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) (n : ℕ) :
    coeff (single 1 n) (lazardSeries a) = if n = 1 then 1 else 0 := by
  simp [coeff_lazardSeries_eq]

/-- The series `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` has constant coefficient zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem constantCoeff_lazardSeries (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) : constantCoeff (lazardSeries a) = 0 := by
  simpa using coeff_single_zero_lazardSeries a 0

/-- Changing coefficients in `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` applies the ring homomorphism to each `aᵢⱼ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_lazardSeries (φ : A →+* B) (a : ℕ+ × ℕ+ → A) :
    map φ (lazardSeries a) = lazardSeries (φ ∘ a) := by
  ext d
  rw [coeff_map, coeff_lazardSeries_eq, coeff_lazardSeries_eq]
  split_ifs <;> simp

end Semiring

variable {A B R S : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing R] [CommRing S]

/-- Every formal group law `F(X, Y)` is the series `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` of its coefficients
`aᵢⱼ`. -/
theorem lazardSeries_coeff_toPowerSeries (F : FormalGroup R) :
    lazardSeries (fun ij ↦ coeff (single 0 (ij.1 : ℕ) + single 1 (ij.2 : ℕ)) F.toPowerSeries) =
      F.toPowerSeries := by
  ext d
  rw [← Finsupp.univ_sum_single d, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  by_cases h : d 0 ≠ 0 ∧ d 1 ≠ 0
  · simp [coeff_lazardSeries_eq, h, Nat.pos_of_ne_zero]
  · obtain h | h := not_and_or.1 h <;> simp_all [F.coeff_single_zero, F.coeff_single_one]

/-- The generic series `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` over `ℤ[aᵢⱼ]`. -/
private abbrev genericSeries : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) (MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ) :=
  lazardSeries MvPolynomial.X

namespace LazardRing

/-- The **Lazard relations**: the ideal of `ℤ[aᵢⱼ | i, j ≥ 1]` generated by the coefficients of
`G(G(X, Y), Z) - G(X, G(Y, Z))` and of `G(X, Y) - G(Y, X)`, where
`G = X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` is the generic series. -/
def relations : Ideal (MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ) :=
  Ideal.span <|
    Set.range (fun d ↦ coeff d (genericSeries.subst ![genericSeries.subst ![X 0, X 1], X 2] -
      genericSeries.subst ![X 0, genericSeries.subst ![X 1, X 2]] :
        MvPowerSeries (Fin 3) (MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ))) ∪
    Set.range (fun d ↦ coeff d (genericSeries - genericSeries.subst ![X 1, X 0]))

/-- A ring homomorphism out of `ℤ[aᵢⱼ]` kills the Lazard relations exactly when the series
`X + Y + ∑ ψ(aᵢⱼ) Xⁱ Yʲ` is associative and commutative. -/
private theorem relations_le_ker_iff (ψ : MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ →+* R) :
    relations ≤ RingHom.ker ψ ↔
      ((lazardSeries (ψ ∘ MvPolynomial.X)).subst
          ![(lazardSeries (ψ ∘ MvPolynomial.X)).subst ![X 0, X 1], X 2] =
        ((lazardSeries (ψ ∘ MvPolynomial.X)).subst
          ![X 0, (lazardSeries (ψ ∘ MvPolynomial.X)).subst ![X 1, X 2]] :
            MvPowerSeries (Fin 3) R) ∧
      lazardSeries (ψ ∘ MvPolynomial.X) =
        (lazardSeries (ψ ∘ MvPolynomial.X)).subst ![X 1, X 0]) := by
  have hG : constantCoeff genericSeries = 0 := constantCoeff_lazardSeries _
  -- Base change commutes with substituting a pair of series into a two-variable series.
  have hmap {σ : Type} (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) _) {p q : MvPowerSeries σ _}
      (h : HasSubst ![p, q]) : map ψ (f.subst ![p, q]) = (map ψ f).subst ![map ψ p, map ψ q] := by
    rw [map_subst h]
    congr 1
    funext i
    fin_cases i <;> rfl
  simp only [relations, Ideal.span_le, Set.union_subset_iff, Set.range_subset_iff,
    SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, ← coeff_map, map_sub,
    hmap _ (HasSubst.cons_subst_zero_left (0 : Fin 3) 1 2 hG),
    hmap _ (HasSubst.cons_subst_zero_right (0 : Fin 3) 1 2 hG), hmap _ HasSubst.X_X, map_X,
    map_lazardSeries, ← MvPowerSeries.ext_iff, sub_eq_zero]

end LazardRing

/-- The **Lazard ring** `L = ℤ[aᵢⱼ | i, j ≥ 1] ⧸ LazardRing.relations`: the quotient of the
polynomial ring on the coefficients `aᵢⱼ` of `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` by the coefficients of
associativity and commutativity. Ring homomorphisms out of it classify commutative formal group
laws (`TauCeti.LazardRing.lift`). -/
def LazardRing : Type := MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ ⧸ LazardRing.relations

instance : CommRing LazardRing :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing (MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ ⧸ LazardRing.relations))

namespace LazardRing

/-- The quotient map `ℤ[aᵢⱼ] →+* LazardRing`. -/
def mk : MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ →+* LazardRing :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk relations

/-- Every element of the Lazard ring is the class of a polynomial in the `aᵢⱼ`. -/
theorem mk_surjective : Function.Surjective mk :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- The kernel of the quotient map `ℤ[aᵢⱼ] →+* LazardRing` is the ideal of Lazard relations. -/
theorem ker_mk : RingHom.ker mk = relations :=
  Ideal.mk_ker

/-- The **universal formal group law** `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` over the Lazard ring, whose
coefficients are the classes of the variables `aᵢⱼ`. -/
def formalGroup : FormalGroup LazardRing where
  toPowerSeries := lazardSeries fun ij ↦ mk (MvPolynomial.X ij)
  zero_constantCoeff := constantCoeff_lazardSeries _
  lin_coeff_X := by simp
  lin_coeff_Y := by simp
  assoc := ((relations_le_ker_iff mk).1 ker_mk.ge).1

/-- The universal formal group law is `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ`, with `aᵢⱼ` the classes of the
variables of `ℤ[aᵢⱼ]` in the Lazard ring. -/
theorem formalGroup_toPowerSeries :
    formalGroup.toPowerSeries = lazardSeries fun ij ↦ mk (MvPolynomial.X ij) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in the universal formal group law is the class of `aᵢⱼ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_formalGroup (i j : ℕ+) :
    coeff (single 0 (i : ℕ) + single 1 (j : ℕ)) formalGroup.toPowerSeries =
      mk (MvPolynomial.X (i, j)) := by
  rw [formalGroup_toPowerSeries, coeff_lazardSeries]

/-- The universal formal group law is commutative. -/
instance : formalGroup.IsComm where
  comm := ((relations_le_ker_iff mk).1 ker_mk.ge).2

/-- The ring homomorphism `ℤ[aᵢⱼ] →+* R` sending `aᵢⱼ` to the coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in `F`. -/
private def coeffHom (F : FormalGroup R) : MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ →+* R :=
  MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom (Int.castRingHom R) fun ij ↦
    coeff (single 0 (ij.1 : ℕ) + single 1 (ij.2 : ℕ)) F.toPowerSeries

private theorem lazardSeries_coeffHom (F : FormalGroup R) :
    lazardSeries (fun ij ↦ coeffHom F (MvPolynomial.X ij)) = F.toPowerSeries := by
  simpa [coeffHom] using lazardSeries_coeff_toPowerSeries F

/-- The ring homomorphism `LazardRing →+* R` sending the class of `aᵢⱼ` to the coefficient of
`Xⁱ Yʲ` in a commutative formal group law `F`. -/
private def liftHom (F : FormalGroup R) [F.IsComm] : LazardRing →+* R :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift relations (coeffHom F) fun _ hx ↦ by
    refine RingHom.mem_ker.1 ((relations_le_ker_iff (coeffHom F)).2 ?_ hx)
    rw [Function.comp_def, lazardSeries_coeffHom]
    exact ⟨F.assoc, FormalGroup.IsComm.comm⟩

private theorem liftHom_mk (F : FormalGroup R) [F.IsComm] (p : MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ) :
    liftHom F (mk p) = coeffHom F p :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk _ _ _

/-- A ring homomorphism out of the Lazard ring is determined by the base change of the universal
formal group law along it. -/
theorem hom_ext {φ ψ : LazardRing →+* R} (h : formalGroup.map φ = formalGroup.map ψ) : φ = ψ := by
  refine (RingHom.cancel_right mk_surjective).1
    (MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r ↦ by simp) fun ⟨i, j⟩ ↦ ?_)
  have := congrArg (fun F ↦ coeff (single 0 (i : ℕ) + single 1 (j : ℕ)) F.toPowerSeries) h
  simp only [FormalGroup.map_toPowerSeries, coeff_map] at this
  simpa using this

/-- **The universal property of the Lazard ring**: commutative formal group laws over `R`
correspond to ring homomorphisms `LazardRing →+* R`. The homomorphism attached to `F` sends the
class of `aᵢⱼ` to the coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in `F`; conversely a homomorphism `φ` gives the base
change of the universal formal group law along `φ`. -/
def lift : {F : FormalGroup R // F.IsComm} ≃ (LazardRing →+* R) where
  toFun F := have := F.2; liftHom F.1
  invFun φ := ⟨formalGroup.map φ, inferInstance⟩
  left_inv F := Subtype.ext <| FormalGroup.ext <| by
    simp [formalGroup_toPowerSeries, Function.comp_def, liftHom_mk, lazardSeries_coeffHom]
  right_inv φ := hom_ext <| FormalGroup.ext <| by
    simp [formalGroup_toPowerSeries, Function.comp_def, liftHom_mk, lazardSeries_coeffHom]

/-- The homomorphism `lift F` sends the class of `aᵢⱼ` to the coefficient of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in `F`. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_mk_X (F : {F : FormalGroup R // F.IsComm}) (ij : ℕ+ × ℕ+) :
    lift F (mk (MvPolynomial.X ij)) =
      coeff (single 0 (ij.1 : ℕ) + single 1 (ij.2 : ℕ)) F.1.toPowerSeries := by
  simp [lift, liftHom_mk, coeffHom]

/-- On polynomials in the `aᵢⱼ`, the homomorphism `lift F` evaluates `aᵢⱼ` at the coefficient of
`Xⁱ Yʲ` in `F`. -/
theorem lift_comp_mk (F : {F : FormalGroup R // F.IsComm}) :
    (lift F).comp mk = (MvPolynomial.aeval fun ij : ℕ+ × ℕ+ ↦
      coeff (single 0 (ij.1 : ℕ) + single 1 (ij.2 : ℕ)) F.1.toPowerSeries).toRingHom :=
  MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r ↦ by simp) fun ij ↦ by simp

/-- The universal formal group law base-changes along `lift F` to `F`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_lift (F : {F : FormalGroup R // F.IsComm}) : formalGroup.map (lift F) = F.1 :=
  congrArg Subtype.val (lift.left_inv F)

/-- The commutative formal group law attached to `φ : LazardRing →+* R` is the base change of the
universal formal group law along `φ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_lift_symm (φ : LazardRing →+* R) : (lift.symm φ).1 = formalGroup.map φ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The universal property is natural in the coefficient ring: the homomorphism classifying the
base change of `F` along `g` is `g` composed with the homomorphism classifying `F`. -/
theorem lift_map (F : FormalGroup R) [F.IsComm] (g : R →+* S) :
    lift ⟨F.map g, inferInstance⟩ = g.comp (lift ⟨F, inferInstance⟩) :=
  hom_ext <| by rw [map_lift, ← FormalGroup.map_comp, map_lift]

/-! ### The grading -/

/-- The homological degree `2 (i + j - 1)` of the coefficient `aᵢⱼ` of `Xⁱ Yʲ` in a formal group
law. -/
def degree (ij : ℕ+ × ℕ+) : ℕ :=
  2 * ((ij.1 : ℕ) + ij.2 - 1)

/-- The coefficient `aᵢⱼ` has homological degree `2 (i + j - 1)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem degree_apply (i j : ℕ+) : degree (i, j) = 2 * ((i : ℕ) + j - 1) :=
  (rfl)

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.weightedGradedAlgebra

/-- **The Lazard relations are homogeneous**: the ideal of `ℤ[aᵢⱼ]` generated by the coefficients
of associativity and commutativity of `X + Y + ∑ aᵢⱼ Xⁱ Yʲ` is homogeneous when `aᵢⱼ` has degree
`2 (i + j - 1)`. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_relations :
    relations.IsHomogeneous (MvPolynomial.weightedHomogeneousSubmodule ℤ degree) := by
  -- Rescaling the universal formal group law by `T²` is classified by `φ : L → L[T]`, which
  -- multiplies the class of `aᵢⱼ` by `T ^ degree (i, j)`.
  let φ : LazardRing →+* Polynomial LazardRing :=
    lift ⟨(formalGroup.map Polynomial.C).rescale (Polynomial.X ^ 2), inferInstance⟩
  have hφ : φ.comp mk = (Polynomial.mapRingHom mk).comp (MvPolynomial.aeval
      fun ij ↦ Polynomial.C (MvPolynomial.X ij) * Polynomial.X ^ degree ij).toRingHom := by
    refine (lift_comp_mk _).trans <| MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r ↦ by simp) fun ⟨i, j⟩ ↦ ?_
    simp [FormalGroup.coeff_rescale]
    ring
  intro n p hp
  have key : MvPolynomial.weightedHomogeneousComponent degree n p ∈ relations := by
    rw [← ker_mk, RingHom.mem_ker, ← MvPolynomial.coeff_aeval_C_X_mul_X_pow]
    rw [← ker_mk, RingHom.mem_ker] at hp
    have := congrArg φ hp
    rw [← RingHom.comp_apply, hφ, map_zero] at this
    simpa using congrArg (fun q ↦ Polynomial.coeff q n) this
  rwa [← MvPolynomial.weightedDecomposition.decompose'_apply] at key

/-- The **grading of the Lazard ring** by homological degree: `Lₙ` consists of the classes of the
polynomials in the `aᵢⱼ` that are homogeneous of degree `n` when `aᵢⱼ` has degree
`2 (i + j - 1)`. -/
def grading (n : ℕ) : Submodule ℤ LazardRing :=
  GradedAlgebra.quotientPiece (MvPolynomial.weightedHomogeneousSubmodule ℤ degree) relations n

/-- An element of the Lazard ring has degree `n` exactly when it is the class of a polynomial in
the `aᵢⱼ` that is homogeneous of degree `n`. -/
theorem mem_grading_iff {n : ℕ} {x : LazardRing} :
    x ∈ grading n ↔ ∃ p : MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ, p.IsWeightedHomogeneous degree n ∧ mk p = x :=
  GradedAlgebra.mem_quotientPiece_iff _ _

/-- The class of a polynomial that is homogeneous of degree `n` has degree `n`. -/
theorem mk_mem_grading {n : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial (ℕ+ × ℕ+) ℤ}
    (hp : p.IsWeightedHomogeneous degree n) : mk p ∈ grading n :=
  mem_grading_iff.2 ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩

/-- Multiplication adds degrees in the Lazard ring. -/
instance : SetLike.GradedMonoid grading :=
  inferInstanceAs (SetLike.GradedMonoid (GradedAlgebra.quotientPiece _ _))

/-- The Lazard ring is the direct sum of its graded pieces `Lₙ`. -/
theorem isInternal_grading : DirectSum.IsInternal grading :=
  GradedAlgebra.isInternal_quotientPiece _ _ isHomogeneous_relations

/-- The Lazard ring is graded by homological degree. -/
instance : GradedAlgebra grading :=
  isInternal_grading.gradedAlgebra

/-- The coefficient of `X^(d 0) Y^(d 1)` in the universal formal group law has degree
`2 (d 0 + d 1 - 1)`. -/
theorem coeff_formalGroup_mem_grading (d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ) :
    coeff d formalGroup.toPowerSeries ∈ grading (2 * (d.degree - 1)) := by
  rw [formalGroup_toPowerSeries, coeff_lazardSeries_eq]
  split_ifs with h h'
  · refine mk_mem_grading ?_
    convert MvPolynomial.isWeightedHomogeneous_X ℤ degree _
    simp [degree_apply, degree_eq_sum, Nat.toPNat'_coe, Nat.pos_of_ne_zero h.1,
      Nat.pos_of_ne_zero h.2]
  · rw [degree_eq_sum, Fin.sum_univ_two, h']
    exact SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := grading)
  · exact zero_mem _

variable {σ : Type*} [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]

/-- **The graded universal property of the Lazard ring**, pointwise: let `A` be graded by `𝒜`
over a commutative monoid `ι` receiving the degrees of `L` along `e : ℕ →+ ι` (for instance
`ι = ℕ` with `e = id`, or `ι = ℤ` with `e` the inclusion or its negative). The homomorphism
`L →+* A` classifying a commutative formal group law `F` over `A` maps each `Lₙ` into `𝒜 (e n)`
exactly when the coefficient of every monomial `X^(d 0) Y^(d 1)` in `F` lies in
`𝒜 (e (2 (d 0 + d 1 - 1)))`. Since the coefficients of `X` and `Y` are `1` and those of the other
monomials `Xⁿ` and `Yⁿ` vanish, this says that the coefficient `aᵢⱼ` of `F` lies in
`𝒜 (e (2 (i + j - 1)))` for all `i, j ≥ 1`. -/
theorem lift_mem_iff {ι : Type*} [AddCommMonoid ι] {𝒜 : ι → σ} [SetLike.GradedMonoid 𝒜]
    (e : ℕ →+ ι) (F : {F : FormalGroup A // F.IsComm}) :
    (∀ ⦃n : ℕ⦄ ⦃x : LazardRing⦄, x ∈ grading n → lift F x ∈ 𝒜 (e n)) ↔
      ∀ d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ, coeff d F.1.toPowerSeries ∈ 𝒜 (e (2 * (d.degree - 1))) := by
  refine ⟨fun h d ↦ ?_, fun h n x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  · rw [← map_lift F, FormalGroup.map_toPowerSeries, coeff_map]
    exact h (coeff_formalGroup_mem_grading d)
  · obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := mem_grading_iff.1 hx
    -- Pushing the degrees forward along `e` preserves weighted homogeneity.
    have hpe : p.IsWeightedHomogeneous (e ∘ degree) (e n) := fun d hd ↦ by
      simp only [← hp hd, Finsupp.weight_apply, map_finsuppSum, map_nsmul, Function.comp_apply]
    -- The pieces are closed under the `ℤ`-action, as `IsWeightedHomogeneous.aeval_mem` requires.
    have := AddSubgroupClass.zsmulMemClass (S := σ) (M := A)
    rw [← RingHom.comp_apply, lift_comp_mk]
    refine hpe.aeval_mem fun ⟨i, j⟩ ↦ ?_
    have hd := h (single 0 (i : ℕ) + single 1 (j : ℕ))
    rwa [map_add, Finsupp.degree_single, Finsupp.degree_single, ← degree_apply] at hd

variable {𝒜 : ℕ → σ} [SetLike.GradedMonoid 𝒜]

/-- **The graded universal property of the Lazard ring**: for a commutative ring `A` graded by
`𝒜`, graded ring homomorphisms `L →+*ᵍ A` correspond to commutative formal group laws over `A`
whose coefficient of every monomial `X^(d 0) Y^(d 1)` lies in `𝒜 (2 (d 0 + d 1 - 1))`, that is,
whose coefficient `aᵢⱼ` lies in `𝒜 (2 (i + j - 1))` for all `i, j ≥ 1`. A formal group law
corresponds to the homomorphism `TauCeti.LazardRing.lift` classifying it. -/
def gradedLift :
    {F : FormalGroup A // F.IsComm ∧ ∀ d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ,
      coeff d F.toPowerSeries ∈ 𝒜 (2 * (d.degree - 1))} ≃ (grading →+*ᵍ 𝒜) where
  toFun F :=
    { toRingHom := lift ⟨F.1, F.2.1⟩
      map_mem := fun hx ↦ (lift_mem_iff (.id ℕ) ⟨F.1, F.2.1⟩).2 F.2.2 hx }
  invFun φ := ⟨formalGroup.map φ.toRingHom, inferInstance,
    (lift_mem_iff (.id ℕ) (lift.symm φ.toRingHom)).1 (by simpa using fun _ _ ↦ φ.map_mem)⟩
  left_inv F := Subtype.ext <| by simp
  right_inv φ := GradedRingHom.ext fun x ↦
    DFunLike.congr_fun (lift.apply_symm_apply φ.toRingHom) x

/-- The graded homomorphism attached to `F` is the homomorphism classifying `F`. -/
@[simp]
theorem toRingHom_gradedLift (F : {F : FormalGroup A // F.IsComm ∧ ∀ d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ,
      coeff d F.toPowerSeries ∈ 𝒜 (2 * (d.degree - 1))}) :
    (gradedLift F).toRingHom = lift ⟨F.1, F.2.1⟩ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The graded homomorphism attached to `F` is, as a function, the homomorphism classifying `F`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_gradedLift (F : {F : FormalGroup A // F.IsComm ∧ ∀ d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ,
      coeff d F.toPowerSeries ∈ 𝒜 (2 * (d.degree - 1))}) :
    ⇑(gradedLift F) = lift ⟨F.1, F.2.1⟩ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The formal group law attached to a graded homomorphism `φ` is the base change of the universal
formal group law along `φ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_gradedLift_symm (φ : grading →+*ᵍ 𝒜) :
    (gradedLift.symm φ).1 = formalGroup.map φ.toRingHom :=
  (rfl)

end LazardRing

end TauCeti
